<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guelowar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gelwaar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Guelowar were a maternal royal lineage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> origin from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu</a> that, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> tradition, settled in the Serer country of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> around the 14th century. Marrying into the old Serer landholding families, they supplied the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-sine">Sine</a> and Saloum, with succession passing through the female line. Their dynasties reigned until the 20th century.</p></div>
